<?xml version='1.0' standalone='yes'?>
<!DOCTYPE PLUGIN [
<!ENTITY name    "undash">
<!ENTITY author  "Stiphr">
<!ENTITY version "0.5.1">
<!ENTITY emhttp  "/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/&name;">
<!ENTITY flash   "/boot/config/plugins/&name;">
<!ENTITY pluginURL "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Stiphr/UnDash/main/undash.plg">
]>
<PLUGIN name="&name;" author="&author;" version="&version;" pluginURL="&pluginURL;" launch="UnDash" min="6.12.0" icon="undash.png" support="https://github.com/Stiphr/UnDash/issues">

<CHANGES>
###0.5.1
- Version numbers are now x.y.z (this is 0.5.1); releases are the vX.Y.Z tags. Plugin users coming from a 2026.x.x date version: reinstall the plugin once, as Unraid compares the old and new numbers as text.
- Title bar: the UnDash logo and name, your server, its Unraid version and the UnDash version, each with an "available" badge when a newer one exists (UnDash checks its GitHub releases at most every 6 hours). The Docker version now shows the server's name and address instead of the container's.
- The same safe margin in every theme (other themes used to get less room than Default on the full-window page); set your own side and top/bottom margins in Settings &gt; Theme &gt; Spacing.
- Search: while filtering, sections and media columns with nothing that matches are hidden instead of showing empty boxes; one line says when nothing matches at all.
- Settings reorganized into grouped pages with a side menu: Layout, Media &amp; downloads, Containers &amp; VMs, Apps, Theme, Custom CSS, Refresh &amp; display, Ignored alerts, Connection, Backup &amp; import. Checkboxes, sliders, dropdown lists and confirmation dialogs now follow the theme.
- Fixes: Fluent's background gradient was lost on the full-window page; the settings group headings lost their style when switching pages.

###2026.11.02d
- Themes: every theme now has a light and a dark version (AMOLED is pure white in light mode, Fluent Dark becomes Fluent Light), so Light / Dark / System always applies.
- Wallpaper: brightness 0-100%, and the blur can cover the whole wallpaper or only what is behind the cards (frosted glass, the picture stays sharp). Text on the wallpaper gets a frosted backing so it stays readable.
- Search box: type a title to find movies and series in Overseerr / Jellyseerr and request them right there (series: all seasons).
- Docker version: the "no dashboard password" alert is red, highlighted and always first.

###2026.11.02c
- Docker version: the first-start page can be skipped ("Continue without a password", no setup code needed); a password is still recommended. Add, change or remove it any time in Settings &gt; Configuration &gt; Dashboard password. While there is none, an alert says so (it can be ignored like any other).
- Setting or changing the password signs out every other browser, including ones that came in while there was no password.

###2026.11.02b
- Docker version: a container stuck in a restart loop is now flagged (the Unraid API reports it as exited with a "Restarting" status). Checked against a real server: Docker mode now reports the same containers, updates, VMs, pools and alerts as the plugin.
- Docker docs: the UPS tile needs apcupsd in Docker mode; a NUT-only UPS is read by the plugin only.

###2026.11.02a
- New sections: Now playing (Plex, Emby, Jellyfin, Tautulli streams with progress, direct play or transcode, quality and bandwidth), Requests (Overseerr / Jellyseerr, approve or decline pending requests) and Endpoint health (status and latency of every app and container web UI, with Re-probe).
- Alert history: when each problem started and ended, checked once a minute in the background (also when no dashboard is open), kept for 30 days. Alerts &gt; History.
- Keyboard shortcuts: / filter, r refresh, p pause, comma settings, ? list, g + letter to jump to a section.
- The Inter typeface is now bundled, so the dashboard looks the same on every computer.
- Fixes: web UI links of containers on a user-defined Docker network with published ports now use the server's address and host port (they pointed at the container's internal address); the filter box now filters Media, Arr Stack and Downloads immediately; quick preference clicks can no longer overwrite each other; scrolled media lists keep their place while columns rebalance; error messages are red again; stale "⋯ menu" hints now say gear.

###2026.11.01b
- Containers and VMs: one gear button per item holds every action (open web UI or console, start / stop, restart, pause, update, logs, details, favorites, customize). Click the icon or the name to open the web UI (VNC console for VMs); the separate open buttons are gone.
- More room in the container grid and the VM list: bigger icons, taller rows, wider gaps.

###2026.11.01a
- Themes: Light / Dark / System mode and ten colour themes: Default, AMOLED, Minimal, Zinc Blue, Kanagawa Wave, Kanagawa Dragon, Catppuccin, Nord, Tokyo Night and Fluent Dark (frosted glass with blue accents). Most have light and dark versions. The accent follows the theme unless you pick your own.
- Smart heights: app cards in a row are the same height, and in the two-column area the shorter column ends level with the taller one (Media shows more items, otherwise the last box stretches).
- Inter-first font stack and 10 px corners, closer to qui's look. Your current theme and accent are unchanged; the old Light theme is now Default in light mode.

###2026.11.01
- Less wasted space: the System tiles and the Apps cards now fill the whole row, app cards are only as tall as their content, and sections sit closer together.
- Half-width sections that follow each other (e.g. Media, Arr Stack, Downloads) are stacked in two balanced columns, so a short section no longer leaves a gap beside a tall one.
- Media shows four columns from a narrower width; in narrow columns the Radarr / Sonarr link shrinks to its icon so the title fits.
- The Launcher section is removed (a saved Launcher entry is dropped from the layout).

###2026.10.31e
- System tiles are separate cards with bigger numbers; CPU, memory, network and disk temperature show their recent history as a small chart under the value.
- New Launcher section (right after System): one-click icons for every app with a link, with a status dot taken from the container of the same name. Hide or move it in Settings &gt; Dashboard.
- App cards: large numbers are shortened (16.9K, exact value on hover), latency is rounded, and labels no longer break mid-word.

###2026.10.31b
- Media: four equal columns (upcoming movies, upcoming episodes, recently added movies, recently added episodes) as compact lists that scroll on their own; 4, 2 or 1 columns depending on the space. Each column has its own item count (Settings &gt; Dashboard &gt; Media).
- Alerts: Ignore on each alert, for 1 hour, 24 hours, 7 days, a custom time or permanently, or for every alert of that type (with a confirmation). Undo right after ignoring. Disk alerts are now per disk.
- Settings &gt; Ignored alerts: temporarily ignored, permanently ignored and ignored alert types, with filter, Restore, Restore all and Delete expired.
- Ignoring only hides an alert; monitoring continues, and an alert comes back when its rule is restored or runs out while the problem is still there. Rules are kept in ignores.json in the configuration folder.

###2026.10.31a
- Apps (Plex, Emby, Tautulli, AdGuard, Immich …) now sit right below Arr Stack and Downloads as one grid of compact cards; group titles and the old Services shortcut links are off by default (Settings &gt; Dashboard &gt; Apps).
- Containers: a compact multi-column grid instead of a full-width table, showing the running containers by default. Pick your own set with "Selected" (⋯ menu or Settings), choose the columns and which details each container shows. Table and card layouts are still there.
- Settings schema 4; existing settings are migrated.

###2026.10.30b
- Redesign: a compact System overview bar first (click a tile for details: per-core CPU, history, disks), then Media, Arr Stack and Download Clients, then containers, VMs and other apps.
- Media: upcoming movies (with cinema / digital / physical release), upcoming episodes, recently added movies and episodes, as poster rows from Radarr and Sonarr.
- Arr Stack: one row per app with online state, key numbers, health warnings and stuck or failed imports.
- Download clients: speeds, active / stalled / queued / paused counts, progress and ETA, pause and resume all.
- Containers: compact rows by default (expanded view available); VMs compact too.
- The Services section is gone: apps appear where they belong (Arr Stack, Downloads, Media), the rest under Apps. Nothing is shown twice.
- Settings: drag to reorder sections, overview tiles and media widgets; compact / comfortable / expanded density.
- New: Docker image that uses the official Unraid API (see the README). The plugin keeps working as before.

###2026.10.29e
- One page for everything: server overview with health and quick actions, alerts, favorites, system metrics, containers, VMs, storage and app widgets. The separate Docker, VMs and System tabs are gone; settings open in a side panel.
- Live refresh every 2 seconds by default (configurable, pause/resume, last update time, reconnects on its own, slows down in background tabs). One light request per refresh; per-container CPU and memory come from cgroups.
- Containers: discovered automatically; start, stop, restart, pause, update, bulk update with progress, logs, details; favorites, custom names, icons and hiding kept by name. "Not checked" is shown separately from "up to date".
- VMs: only the actions that fit the VM's state are offered; graceful shutdown and force stop are separate and confirmed.
- Restart and shut down the server from the dashboard (type the server name to confirm; Unraid's own commands).
- More metrics: per-core CPU, swap, array capacity and disk health, load, host and address, container and VM totals, UPS.
- Three themes (Default, Light, AMOLED), custom accent colour, density, custom CSS editor with live preview.
- Settings live in /mnt/user/appdata/undash (configurable, mirrored to the flash drive), with automatic backups and restore.
- Export (full or redacted without secrets), import with a preview, configuration check.
- UnDash on its own port (default 9099) for browsers signed in to Unraid.

###2026.10.29
- First release: a Homepage-style dashboard that runs as a native Unraid plugin (no Docker container).
- System cards and top bar from the kernel and Unraid's own state: CPU, memory, disk, network, temperature, uptime, UPS (NUT or apcupsd).
- Docker: start, stop, restart, pause/resume, update (Unraid's own update_container), update all, check for updates, live logs.
- VMs: start, stop, force stop, restart, pause/resume, hibernate, VNC console.
- Unraid OS: shows the installed version, checks for a newer release and installs it from the dashboard.
- Widgets for Radarr, Sonarr, Lidarr, Readarr, Bazarr, Prowlarr, Overseerr/Jellyseerr, Autobrr, Wizarr, qBittorrent, SABnzbd, Emby, Jellyfin, Plex, Tautulli, AdGuard, Pi-hole, Nginx Proxy Manager, Immich, PeaNUT, calendars and custom JSON APIs.
- Import from a gethomepage/homepage services.yaml, settings.yaml and .env.
</CHANGES>

